node_modules/
dist/
/out/
data/
*.log
.DS_Store
.env
.env.local
# Local AI working state stays local (codemap index, memory, launch config, harnesses) - but the
# SLASH COMMANDS ship: they are how a person operates this daemon, and a rule that lives on one
# machine is not a rule the team has. Same idiom as .arkitect below.
/.claude/*
!/.claude/commands/
# Architect: run output stays local; the config + custom checks (your-checks/) are committed
# owner-owned tooling (the reusable guardrail checks live there). The core is fetched by npx.
.arkitect/*
!.arkitect/arkitect.config.json
!.arkitect/your-checks/
tmp/
PLAN.md

# tray launcher: the .lnk stores absolute paths - regenerate it per machine with
# misc/New-TrayShortcut.ps1 (the tray host refreshes it on launch)
/AgentHydra.lnk
/AgentHydra Instances.lnk
# The pre-rename shortcuts survive on machines that upgraded, until they are re-created.
/CCManagerUI.lnk
/CCManagerUI Instances.lnk

# Local root rebuild convenience wrapper (delegates to misc/Rebuild.bat)
/Rebuild.bat

# Owner handoff notes: internal, not for the public repo
docs/HANDOFF_MICHAEL.md

# Local AI memory for this repo. Deliberately NOT published.
/.claude/memory/

# ⛔ PUBLIC REPO: the to-do list is not published (owner directive, 2026-08-29).
# These notes are the most candid writing in the repo - what is broken, what is half-built, what is
# waiting on a person - and Odin's Loki files them here automatically from chat history. The
# folder's own README stays tracked (it is already tracked, and it states the convention); only the
# items are ignored. Managed by public_todo_guard.py in the Odin repo.
/docs/todo/*
!/docs/todo/README.md

# bun test --parallel writes a per-file timing cache here to schedule the next run.
/timings.json

# A built or downloaded binary dropped at the repo root. `bun run dist` writes the real one to
# dist/ (ignored above); this is the copy people leave beside the checkout after downloading a
# release asset or hand-copying one out of dist/. It is ~100 MB, so an accidental `git add` here
# is expensive and irreversible on a public repo. Named exactly, NOT as a blanket *.exe, because
# misc/lunarwerx-tray.exe is a tracked, committed part of the tray toolkit.
/AgentHydra.exe

# Local investigation write-ups: internal working notes, same convention as
# docs/HANDOFF_MICHAEL.md and /docs/todo/* above. Findings get upstreamed as a fix plus its
# comment, not as a file of field notes about one machine's logs.
/FINDINGS-*.md
